id: pm-vcs-p7objects
title: First-class conflict objects stored in changes
description: "Opt-in merge recording stores one content-addressed object per conflicting structured field or text hunk, referenced by the tree alongside readable merged content. Existing fail-on-conflict behavior is preserved. Includes explicit tip resolution."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:01:39.215Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T10:27:19.077Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "Conflict units preserve base/ours/theirs and independent edits merge; conflicted snapshots remain committable and transportable; status/show/log/items report units in TOON and JSON; verify, GC, erasure and bounded history retain or safely deny the complete closure; real tracker proof and behavioural revert proofs pass unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
parent: pm-vcs-phase7
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T03:02:09.086Z",codex-agent,"Plan: preserve legacy merge behavior by default and under --fail-on-conflict. Add explicit --record-conflicts so automation opts in without changing existing callers. Store per-unit conflict addresses on tree/index entries beside a readable ours projection, never marker text. Ship tip resolve in this slice; ancestor resolution and automatic descendant propagation remain child pm-vcs-p7resolve. No release workflows will change."
  "2026-10-18T03:08:24.490Z",codex-agent,"Implemented canonical field/hunk conflict objects, versioned tree/index references, explicit merge recording, tip resolve, conflict reporting and lifecycle traversal. Verification is in progress against real PM trackers, two linked working trees and bounded transfers. Ancestor propagation remains deferred to pm-vcs-p7resolve. Pinned pm is 2026.10.13; current published pm is 2026.10.17; the pin is unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T03:23:35.824Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs in an isolated source copy: reverting only the mergePath body to origin/main makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^field objects preserve\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fail 0/1 with unsupported_recorded_conflict because unit references disappear. Reverting only collectCommitObjects makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^bundle, push/fetch\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fail 0/1 with incomplete_bundle and two missing conflict objects. Tests import production TypeScript directly; no dist rebuild is involved. Both bodies were restored after each controlled proof."
  "2026-10-18T03:43:38.262Z",codex-agent,"Verification before final release gates: the linked full conflict regression command passed 14/14 with zero failed, skipped or cancelled tests, including real PM_AUTHOR worktrees, readable native items, two continuing agents, third-author resolution, packed CLI TOON/JSON, native Bun reads, real HTTP push/fetch, GC, partial history and erasure. The subsequently added EOF/newline and metadata-only resolution cases passed 2/2 through the linked runner. Native PM round-trip rejection passed 1/1 and refuses a lossy body value before moving HEAD. Linked result tracking is disabled by existing repository policy, so these receipts are recorded here without changing that policy. Controlled revert proofs are in the preceding comment. Full npm/Bun gate and CI receipts will be published in the PR for this branch; no release is approved."
  "2026-10-18T03:52:33.160Z",codex-agent,"Final retention checks passed for repeated contenders, resolution merges in both directions, moves/copies retaining stable file identities and independent conflict state, and exact structured field names. Repeated-field side selection now refuses ambiguity and requires --value. Field handling treats only own document/policy properties as values, including prototype-named keys. Structured resolution validates a lossless native-format round trip before publishing refs. No CLI/SDK defect requiring an upstream change was found; the pinned host correctly required isolated/snapshot workspace mode for pm_context_mode=none, so linked runs retained the existing schema context. Final npm/Bun gates and CI remain pending."
  "2026-10-18T04:23:13.816Z",codex-agent,"First-head CI exposed an export discovery regression, a stale production inventory assertion, and three uncovered metadata-retention branches. Bundle discovery now requests manifest/conflict kinds in one bounded prefix scan; the unchanged strace regression passes with one serialized payload hash pass plus 64 discovery bytes. The all-source inventory increases from 65 to 66 for engine/conflicts.ts without changing thresholds or exclusions. Idempotent/descendant merge and restore regressions cover the missing retained-unit branches. Node 26 first-head CI was 1570/1584 and Node 22 was 1569/1584, zero skips; their erasure setup refusals are addressed under existing pm-vcs-simi with a deterministic independently failing proof. Final gates will rerun on the repaired head."
  "2026-10-18T04:29:14.990Z",codex-agent,"Tightened recorded-conflict validation to require each fresh disagreement itself to be represented, so an inherited unit cannot hide a new mode, identity or payload-kind conflict on the same path. The structural regression and retained-unit/PID checks pass 3/3; build:test passes. Reverting only the new guard condition makes the structural regression fail 0/1 with a missing expected exception. This preserves explicit structural reconciliation and leaves no stopped merge state. Final exact-head gates follow this repair."
  "2026-10-18T06:34:16.425Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #122: read all three unresolved CodeRabbit threads and open reviewer issues #123 and #124. The current per-disagreement recorded flag already rejects unsupported structural merges; extend production Repository tests to cover delete/edit and mode changes with and without inherited field/text units. Fix overlapping text resolution by rejecting ambiguous side selections and applying one explicit replacement per connected disputed range, preserving independent text and EOF state. Review erasure references and items tree-cache reuse, then record behavioural revert proofs and isolated npm/Bun release gates. No dependency changes planned."
  "2026-10-18T06:39:48.244Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs using production TypeScript and real temporary PM repositories: reverting only resolvePayload to the pre-review body makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^collapsed text|^three sibling|^explicit text values\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fail 0/3 (missing ambiguous_resolution). Reverting only region coalescing makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^explicit text values\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fail 0/1: a three-line explicit choice incorrectly leaves a duplicated two-line tail. Restoring only the defective path-has-any-units predicate makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^structural delete\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fail four inherited field/text incoming-delete and mode scenarios (8 passing child cases, 4 failing child cases; aggregate 8 pass/5 fail including parent). The current per-disagreement recorded guard was already present in e56d356; these new Repository.merge tests verify it and snapshot HEAD/index/disk/mode/merge-state/operations on refusal. Reverting only the items cache argument makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^items conflict summaries\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fail 0/1 (two root-tree decodes instead of one). All temporary source changes were restored. Erasure reference cleanup is representation-only: former consumers read IDs only, so it has no behavioural revert failure; existing complete FileId erasure and shared-reference refusal tests remain the acceptance evidence, without an implementation-mirroring test."
  "2026-10-18T06:41:22.064Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation: pm test pm-vcs-p7objects --run --progress --only-index 1 passed all 42 first-class conflict tests, including 12 structural subcases, packed CLI, real HTTP transfer, erasure, repeated fields, disjoint unequal hunk lengths and EOF choices. Linked-test result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment retains the receipt. Lint, zero-duplication and docstring checks passed. Next: unchanged npm and Bun release gates under fresh HOME/global/system Git identity isolation, committed self-host equality and clean-clone strict health; then push and reply to the three threads and issues #123/#124. No history rewriting or dependency refresh was performed."
  "2026-10-18T07:14:52.183Z",codex-agent,"First isolated npm release gate: all 1605 tests passed with zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs, but the unchanged per-file 100% gate correctly refused one uncovered EOF fallback branch in engine/conflicts.ts (99.31% branches there; every other source dimension/file was 100%). Added a real ordinary-truncation regression: a previously non-final inherited hunk becomes EOF, and side resolution must preserve the current projection newline state with and without a trailing newline. No runtime code or thresholds changed. Re-run both complete release gates after this acceptance addition."
  "2026-10-18T07:41:17.319Z",codex-agent,"Final npm run release:check passed on source commit 460b294: 1606/1606 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs. Fresh HOME plus GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 isolated identity. Unchanged c8 --all --100 --per-file measured all 66 source files at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines: 22962 statements and lines, 777 functions, 6965 branches, all covered. Lint, zero duplicates, docstrings, native TOON, stat-cache, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, pack dry run, changelog and release-policy validators all passed. The independent Bun rerun is still in progress. The initial Bun run matched npm: all 1605 tests passed and only the uncovered EOF fallback prevented its release gate. The added real truncation test addresses that coverage gap without runtime changes or threshold reductions."
  "2026-10-18T07:43:19.659Z",codex-agent,"Independent Bun rerun on 460b294 passed all 1606 tests, all 66 source files at 100% in every coverage dimension, and native TOON/stat-cache/self-host/production audit/identity audit/pack checks. The release command then correctly refused changelog validation because the separate checkout was shallow (E_MISSING_TAG_HISTORY). This was a validation setup error, not a package defect. Re-running the complete unchanged Bun release gate in the full-history package worktree with fresh HOME and isolated global/system Git identity; no source changes are needed."
  "2026-10-18T08:00:39.534Z",codex-agent,"Final full-history bun run release:check passed on source commit 460b2947d10b41f3df8080311f5ee40063211d91: 1606/1606 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs; all 66 source files at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines with unchanged --all --100 --per-file thresholds. All remaining acceptance, self-host, audit, packaging, changelog and release-policy checks passed. npm and Bun now both have complete green release commands under fresh HOME/global/system Git identity isolation. The 43 first-class-conflict cases include 12 real structural branch scenarios and the EOF truncation case. All three review threads are addressed; issues #123/#124 have real-engine coverage and independent behavioural revert receipts above. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was found; linked-test result tracking remains disabled by existing policy. Releasing the claim without closing the item. The final receipt commit changes only tracker evidence and its self-host archive; runtime/test source remains identical to 460b294. Current-head CI and reviewer replies will be linked from PR #122 and its checks page after pushing; the PR and threads remain open for orchestrator/reviewer verification."
  "2026-10-18T08:14:17.683Z",codex-agent,"Final range review identified an additional EOF ownership edge within #124: after ordinary deletion, a nonempty inherited range can end where a later zero-width inherited range sits at EOF. The current original-line-count condition lets an earlier unit overwrite the later region newline choice. Reclaiming this item to reproduce the producer through real branch merges and protect the final region ownership before completing the round."
  "2026-10-18T08:16:45.655Z",codex-agent,"Additional EOF producer confirmed and fixed: a first recorded final-line disagreement is followed by a second append disagreement, then an ordinary deletion leaves ranges [1,2) and [2,2). Resolving theirs previously lost the final newline; base could also inherit the earlier unit newline incorrectly. Only the rightmost selected region at EOF now owns termination. All ours/theirs/base choices pass through the real Repository. Behavioural revert: remove only index === 0 from the EOF condition; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^a final zero-width\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fails 0/1 with a missing trailing newline. Restored guard passes 1/1; the full conflict suite passes 44/44, and fresh module-scoped c8 measures engine/conflicts.ts at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Lint/zero-duplication/docstring checks pass. Previous head 8e65907 CI passed, but this new source fix requires both complete release gates and fresh CI; old-head CI is not treated as acceptance of the new source."
  "2026-10-18T08:42:03.384Z",codex-agent,"Final acceptance after the EOF ownership fix: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check passed on 2540c24604364ae2cc2eb0879c97bab9135261dd, each 1607/1607 with zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs. Both used full Git history and fresh HOME/global/system identity isolation. All 66 intended source files retain 100% statements/branches/functions/lines under unchanged --all --100 --per-file thresholds; measured npm totals are 22963 statements/lines, 777 functions and 6969 branches, all covered. Every remaining acceptance, self-host, audit, packaging, changelog and release-policy gate passed. The complete conflict suite is 44/44. The additional EOF-owner-only revert fails 0/1 as recorded above; structural guard, overlapping-range refusal/coalescing and cache reverts retain their independent red proofs. Releasing the claim without closing the feature. The next receipt commit changes only tracker evidence and its self-host archive; source/tests remain byte-identical to 2540c24. A fresh clone will verify strict health, then the updated PR/replies and current-head CI receipt will be maintained at PR #122 and its checks page. CodeRabbit itself auto-resolved the original threads after the earlier replies; no thread was manually resolved by this agent."
  "2026-10-18T09:43:45.992Z",codex-agent,"New review round on fc0cbd0: preserve completed issue #123/#124 fixes and receipts. Address two new threads: reject novel conflict roots attached to permanently erased FileIds, and preserve raw --value whitespace/empty strings at the CLI boundary. Add real-repository regressions with narrow behavioral revert proofs, run both unchanged release gates under isolated Git identity, push and reply, then wait for CI. Branch is current with origin and contains origin/main; no merge or receipt reconciliation is needed."
  "2026-10-18T09:50:55.628Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 behavioral revert proofs: (1) remove only the new conflict-root/FileId guard in assertArrivalsAllowed, leaving all tests and other production code fixed: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"bundle arrivals cannot attach\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts fails both field/text child scenarios (0/3 aggregate), because importBundle publishes the forbidden tree instead of throwing file_obliterated. Restored guard accepts historical erased roots and unrelated FileIds while rejecting a novel root alone or in either order with an inherited root; refusal preserves refs, index, HEAD, operations, denial registry and object inventory. (2) restore only optionalString(context.options, \"value\") in vcs resolve, rebuild, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"resolve command preserves raw|packed CLI resolves literal\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts: 0/2 pass, both handler and real packed CLI return line without its requested EOF newline. Restored raw-value reader and rebuilt. Eleven valid value cases cover empty text deletion, empty/spaced/whitespace-only fields and text, EOF newline, quoted strings and JSON false/null/42. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstrings pass."
  "2026-10-18T09:55:39.097Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 additional arrival controls pass (3/3 aggregate): historical erased roots remain transferable, independent FileIds accept novel alternatives, and an erased FileId cannot adopt a conflict already held for another identity; wrong-owner denied roots retain invalid_erasure_role. Tracker-linked run initially hit its default 120-second packed-consumer timeout after engine/handler assertions passed; the linked test now has a 600-second budget and is rerunning. Result tracking remains disabled, so receipts are retained in comments. Both fixes and narrow revert proofs are ready for full isolated npm/Bun release checks."
  "2026-10-18T10:21:04.820Z",codex-agent,"Full npm gate exposed an existing switch/private-layer refusal defect: a status-driven stat-cache refresh mutates raw index before layer preflight. It reproduces under isolated Git identity; the ordinary targeted run passed because warm cache observations masked the write. Stopped both owned gate runs before changing source; neither interrupted run is acceptance evidence. Tracking the necessary gate repair in pm-vcs-switch-cache with a deterministic cold-index regression and a separate ordering-only revert proof."
  "2026-10-18T10:27:19.077Z",codex-agent,"Final-source repeat confirms both review fixes independently: remove only the new conflict-root/FileId guard -> 0/3 pass, both real field/text bundle imports bypass refusal; restore only the old value reader and rebuild -> 0/2 pass, real handler and packed CLI lose EOF newline. All three fixes are restored and rebuilt. The gate-discovered preflight cache repair is tracked in pm-vcs-switch-cache, with 7/7 real aged-cold-index refusal scenarios and an independent guard-only revert proof; public status cache warming still passes 1/1. Restarting both unchanged isolated release gates from the next committed head; interrupted runs are excluded from acceptance."
